@startuml Create Bulletin Post Flow

title Architecture Bulletin - Create Post and Upload Attachments

actor Admin
participant "React App\n(PostForm)" as Form
participant "PostService" as Service
participant "GitHubDataService\n(Octokit)" as GitHub
participant "GitHub API" as API
participant "Data Repo" as Repo

== Admin Creates New Post ==

Admin -> Form: Clicks "Create New Post"
activate Form

Form --> Admin: Show empty form

Admin -> Form: Fills in:\n- Title\n- Description\n- Concerned Parties\n- Select architects\n- Select status\n- Attach files (2 files)

Admin -> Form: Clicks "Create Post"

Form -> Form: Validate form data:\n- Title required\n- Description required\n- Concerned Parties required\n- Files < 10MB each

alt Validation fails
    Form --> Admin: Show validation errors
else Validation succeeds

    Form -> Form: Show loading state

    Form -> Service: createPost(postData, files)
    activate Service

    Service -> Service: Generate post ID:\npost-XXXX (auto-increment)

    Service -> Service: Prepare post JSON:\n{\n  id, title, description,\n  concernedParties,\n  status, assignedArchitects,\n  createdAt, createdBy,\n  attachments: []\n}

    Service -> GitHub: createFile(\n  path: "posts/post-XXXX.json",\n  content: <base64 JSON>,\n  message: "Create post: {title}"\n)
    activate GitHub

    GitHub -> API: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/posts/post-XXXX.json\nAuthorization: token {token}\n{\n  content: <base64>,\n  message: "Create post: {title}"\n}
    activate API

    API -> Repo: Create file\nposts/post-XXXX.json
    activate Repo
    Repo -> Repo: Git commit created:\n"Create post: {title}\nBy: admin-user"
    Repo --> API: {commit: {sha}, content: {sha}}
    deactivate Repo

    API --> GitHub: 201 Created\n{content, commit}
    deactivate API

    GitHub --> Service: Success\n{postId, postSha}
    deactivate GitHub

    == Upload Attachments ==

    loop For each file (2 files)

        Service -> Service: Prepare file:\n- filename: "diagram.png"\n- base64 encode content\n- path: "attachments/post-XXXX/diagram.png"

        Service -> GitHub: createFile(\n  path: "attachments/post-XXXX/diagram.png",\n  content: <base64 file>,\n  message: "Upload attachment for post-XXXX"\n)
        activate GitHub

        GitHub -> API: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/\nattachments/post-XXXX/diagram.png\n{\n  content: <base64>,\n  message: "Upload attachment for post-XXXX"\n}
        activate API

        API -> Repo: Create file in\nattachments/post-XXXX/
        activate Repo
        Repo --> API: 201 Created
        deactivate Repo

        API --> GitHub: {content: {path, sha, size}}
        deactivate API

        GitHub --> Service: Success\n{attachmentPath, sha}
        deactivate GitHub

        Service -> Service: Add attachment metadata:\n{\n  filename: "diagram.png",\n  path: "attachments/post-XXXX/diagram.png",\n  size: 524288,\n  uploadedBy: "admin-user",\n  uploadedAt: "2025-11-18T10:05:00Z",\n  type: "image/png"\n}

    end

    == Update Post with Attachment Metadata ==

    Service -> Service: Update post JSON:\nAdd attachments array

    Service -> GitHub: updateFile(\n  path: "posts/post-XXXX.json",\n  content: <updated JSON>,\n  sha: <existing post sha>,\n  message: "Add attachments to post-XXXX"\n)
    activate GitHub

    GitHub -> API: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/contents/posts/post-XXXX.json\n{\n  content: <base64>,\n  sha: <existing>,\n  message: "Add attachments"\n}
    activate API

    API -> Repo: Update file\nposts/post-XXXX.json
    activate Repo
    Repo --> API: 200 OK
    deactivate Repo

    API --> GitHub: {content, commit}
    deactivate API

    GitHub --> Service: Success
    deactivate GitHub

    Service --> Form: Post created successfully\n{post: {...}}
    deactivate Service

    Form -> Form: Update PostsContext:\nAdd new post to state

    Form --> Admin: Show success message:\n"Post created successfully"

    Form -> Form: Navigate to PostDetailPage(postId)

    Form --> Admin: Redirect to post detail page
end

deactivate Form

== Error Handling ==

note over Admin, Repo
  Possible errors:
  - File size > 10MB: Show error before upload
  - GitHub API error: Show "Failed to create post"
  - Rate limit exceeded: Show "Rate limit exceeded, try again later"
  - Network error: Show "Network error, please retry"
  - Invalid token: Redirect to login
end note

@enduml
